  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 120 AM MDT THU OCT 29 2026\nShowers will continue through Sunday, tapering off throughout the \nday as the system departs, with QPF details in the short-term. Snow \nlevels Sunday will have lowered to 4.5-6.5kft MSL (increasing from \nwest to east), allowing for a chance of snow/wintry mix down to\naround 4.5 kft MSL Sunday in E-Oregon, with little to no \naccumulation expected that low. Sunday afternoon and evening \nwill feature gusty winds following the cold frontal passage, \nwith west to northwest gusts of 20-40 mph (strongest in the \ntypical windy portions of the Snake River Plain. \n\nBeginning Monday, the area will be dry with a warming trend through \nThursday, although seasonable temperatures are anticipated \nthroughout. While there will be multiple opportunities for weak \nshortwaves to pass over the area, moisture will be limited and the \nshortwaves will just result in periods of increased high clouds.",
